@page "/not-found"

<PageTitle>Page not found</PageTitle>

@*
    Reached by the status-code middleware, not by the router's <NotFound> block: in a Blazor Web
    App that block only covers client-side routing, so a server-rendered miss returned a bare 404
    with an empty body. That is how six unported pages hid — /upload-files looked blank rather
    than missing.
*@

<div class="text-center py-5">
    <h1 class="display-6">Page not found</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mb-4">There is nothing at this address.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Back to the home page</a>
</div>
